  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nFloorp is an open-source web browser made in Japan, privacy focused..\n\nPressing any of the RED confirm/action buttons within the homarr interface on latest Floorp often will just SPIN animation the button and never complete the operation.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRunning Windows 10 Floorp Version 12.14.2@151.0 with default settings, open management in homarr, and try to upload images or edit/remove CSS, any RED button  may spin and never finish the task.\n\n### Impact\n\nmakes you think something is running, but in fact it is not. \nTrying on chrome or doing a few F5 refresh clears for few times, but then it locks up later.\n\n### Additional information\n\n<img width=\"463\" height=\"339\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a7551403-e724-4e3d-b0db-426f0db27bca\" />\n\n### Version\n\n1.69.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\n_No response_",
